   "source": [
    "# Quiz: Build a Cuisine Recommender Web App\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-4-4-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Recommendation systems might be used for</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Recommending a good restaurant</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Recommending fashions to try</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Both of these</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-4-4-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Embedding a model in a web app helps it to be offline-capable</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>true</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. With Onnx, you can use a model inside a web app, and even run it offline if needed.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>false</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A model inside a web app can run locally, and even offline if needed.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-4-4-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Onnx Runtime can be used for</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Running models in a web app</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Onnx Runtime is used to run Onnx models. Your web app uses it to run your saved model.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Training models</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. You train the model first and convert it for Onnx. Onnx Runtime then runs that model.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Hyperparameter tuning</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Onnx Runtime is used to run Onnx models, such as the saved model your web app loads.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-4-4-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Netron app helps you:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Visualize data</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. You open your model.onnx file in Netron to see the model itself, with its inputs and classifier.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Visualize your model's structure</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Netron visualizes your model, so you can check that it is properly built.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Test your web app</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. You test the web app by serving it with http-server. Netron is a tool to view your models.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-4-4-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Convert your Scikit-learn model for use with Onnx using:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>sklearn-app</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. You use sklearn-onnx, installed as skl2onnx, to turn a Scikit-learn model into Onnx format.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>sklearn-web</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The converter is sklearn-onnx, which you install as skl2onnx. It turns a Scikit-learn model into Onnx format.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>sklearn-onnx</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. This converter, installed as skl2onnx, turns your Scikit-learn model into Onnx format.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-4-4-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Using your model in a web app is called:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>inference</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Using your model in a web app, like the cuisine app, is called inference.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>interference</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The word is inference, as in using your model in a web app for inference.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>insurance</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Running your model in a web app to get a result is called inference.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
